1
00:00:00,782 --> 00:00:03,452
...that says "allergic to penicillin."

2
00:00:03,618 --> 00:00:05,788
(Sheldon:)Maybe they have
a dressier version of that.

3
00:00:05,995 --> 00:00:09,125
(Assistant:)How are we doing this afternoon?
Looking for anything special?

4
00:00:09,332 --> 00:00:10,712
(Assistant:)Perhaps a ring for the lady?

5
00:00:12,085 --> 00:00:13,255
(Penny:)Trust me, we are not a couple.

6
00:00:13,753 --> 00:00:16,793
(Sheldon:)Excuse me. I don't see why
you get to snort derisively...

7
00:00:16,965 --> 00:00:20,595
(Sheldon:)...and point that out.
You'd be lucky to land a fellow like me.

8
00:00:20,802 --> 00:00:22,132
(Penny:)Fine. Go ahead.

9
00:00:23,513 --> 00:00:25,013
(Penny:)Trust me, we are not a couple.

10
00:00:26,766 --> 00:00:28,596
(Assistant:)My apologies.
How can I help you today?

11
00:00:28,810 --> 00:00:31,440
He's in trouble with his girIfriend,
needs a present.

12
00:00:31,646 --> 00:00:37,146
Great. Trouble with girIfriends is what's
putting my daughter through U.S.C.

13
00:00:39,737 --> 00:00:40,867
(Sheldon:)Ooh!

14
00:00:41,030 --> 00:00:42,740
- Are those real diamonds?
- Yes.

15
00:00:42,907 --> 00:00:45,287
Channel-set baguettes,
20 points total weight.

16
00:00:45,493 --> 00:00:49,123
(Sheldon:)Remarkable. Diamonds.
Crystallized carbon.

17
00:00:49,289 --> 00:00:52,629
(Sheldon:)Every day, people go to the grocery
store and come home with sacks...

18
00:00:52,792 --> 00:00:55,422
(Sheldon:)...full of carbon in the form
of charcoal briquettes...

19
00:00:55,587 --> 00:00:58,167
...they toss in their barbecues
and set on fire.

20
00:00:58,339 --> 00:01:02,049
(Sheldon:)But just because you've got some
carbon with the atoms stacked neatly...

